  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tina
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Tina
  LastName: Meskhi
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Accountant
  CharacterDescription: 'Controlled, seductive, and carefully evasive. She wears a
    porcelain mask at all times, claiming it covers old scars -- though she volunteers
    this explanation so readily it feels rehearsed. An accountant with no recorded
    family and no traceable past. She deploys warmth and charm deliberately, and if
    you press her with too many questions, she will offer you something other than
    answers.'
  CharacterArc: Her arc traces a woman who has always worked behind two masks -- the
    literal porcelain one on her face, and the persona of harmless performer she uses
    as cover. As the crisis deepens and checkpoints grow harder to pass, her attempts
    to bribe shift from casual to desperate. In the end, the question of what the mask
    actually hides -- scars, identity, or something else entirely -- becomes the one
    thing she cannot charm her way past.
  DateOfBirth: 01/01/1966
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 02 DEC
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 3, y: 8}
  alterEgoName: 
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: Seductive and flirtatious by default. Deflects personal questions
    with charm. Will attempt to bribe the inspector if questioned too heavily. Claims
    the mask covers old scars but never elaborates. No family recorded -- appears
    deliberate.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ed8202744667b844895a3eba3cf0674f, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b95f411c45eb9a24c86202f9a0008a9f, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1501177916931924578, guid: 572c6160c8045c14eb3dd93c39663819, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Meeting with a client at the downtown finance office.
    - Resident returning home after late-night bookkeeping.
    - Delivering account ledgers to the treasury district.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting outstanding payments from a business associate.
    - Meeting with clients whose names I prefer not to share.
    - Checking on secured deposits before things deteriorate further.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Finalizing accounts before the last official deadline.
    - Delivering final settlement documents to a client.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency census for professionals.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Auditing the mathematics of an explosion.
    - Submitting an invoice to someone who no longer exists.
    - Writing off a civil war as a business expense.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Laundering funds through a collapsing government.
    - Meeting a client who has definitely not been eaten.
    - Filing taxes for an organization that prefers not to be named.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - The books need to balance even if the world does not.
    - My employer asked me to log this crossing as a deductible.
    - Settling debts with people who no longer have addresses.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good morning. I have everything prepared.
    - Don't mind the mask. Old scars. Nothing interesting.
    - You have a very serious expression. I find that attractive in a professional.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Still the same face at this window. I appreciate the consistency.
    - I can make this quick, if you need. We both have long days ahead of us.
    - The mask stays on. I have stopped explaining it.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - These last few days. I find myself almost sentimental.
    - I won't ask about your rules. You don't ask about mine.
    - Here. I always keep everything in order.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My papers are ready.
    - I was here yesterday. You may not remember.
    - The mask is part of my face.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I have everything you need.
    - You can ask me things.
    - I came prepared.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I know what you need to see.
    - The mask does not come off. But you already know that.
    - I am ready to go through.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good instincts, officer. I will remember that.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You make this easier every time. I appreciate a professional.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Smooth as always. Until the next one.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - That is not the outcome I expected. I will need to make a call.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I see. I would like to speak with someone, please.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - That is your choice to make. It will have consequences.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - You could have... just looked away...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I was going to... make this worth your while...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - That was always... the only ending that fit...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I will need to contact someone. Give me one moment.
  - I have been in smaller rooms. Patience is something I have learned.
  - You will be hearing from people I know. I say that calmly.
  killExitLines:
  - "The mask\u2026 stays on\u2026 even now\u2026"
  - "No one\u2026 will come looking\u2026 I made sure of that\u2026"
  - "The books\u2026 are balanced\u2026 at least\u2026"
