  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 17a505de1618c134e80b6cf6fb35be35, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5b17e3fdf6196354dad34cc70d2ac032, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: A meeting. The kind that does not appear in schedules.
    midDaysAnswer: I have been moving between locations. No fixed place right now.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere specific. I was just walking.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The theater. Morning rehearsal. Long session. My throat
      is still raw from it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My office. Full day. One meeting after another. Everything
      completely as normal.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The Grand Theater. Still performing. The stage is still
      standing. Someone has to keep it running.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: I was already here.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: I came from the same place I always come from.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I don't remember exactly. But I arrived.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing worth mentioning.
    midDaysAnswer: "I sleep less. I\u2019ve stopped noticing that I sleep less. You
      get used to things."
    finalDaysAnswer: "I don\u2019t feel much of anything lately. I\u2019ve decided
      to call that stability."
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: I feel perfectly well. Better than usual, honestly.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: "No symptoms. Nothing. I am sharp, focused. I don\u2019t
      know how, but I am."
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My health is excellent. Full range. Everything working
      exactly as it should.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: No.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: I don't think so.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I can't tell anymore.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: "No one. I\u2019ve always preferred it that way. Nothing recorded,
      either."
    midDaysAnswer: I have been moving. No fixed arrangement.
    finalDaysAnswer: Alone. Still alone.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Two colleagues. A shared arrangement near the theater
      district.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: A full household. Very comfortable. Plenty of company.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: "Everyone is still there. All of them. The flat is full.
      It\u2019s fine."
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: No one.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I don't know anymore.
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - You keep staring at the mask. Most people have the manners not to.
    - You are very thorough. I find that attractive in this line of work.
    - The family section is blank on purpose. You can note that down if you like.
    midDays:
    - I could make this easier for both of us, if you are the right kind of professional.
    - The mask is not decorative. But it is not medically relevant either. It is simply
      mine.
    - You have a good instinct for your job. I respect people with instincts.
    finalDays:
    - By now we know each other, in the way checkpoints make you know people.
    - I have no next of kin to list. That has always been deliberate.
    - Ask what you need to ask. I am not in any particular hurry.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 6703375
